{"name":"South Rim Trail","hex":"#a6847b","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"south","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The direction towards the pole to the right-hand side of someone facing east, specifically 180°, or (on another celestial object) the direction towards the pole lying on the southern side of the invariable plane.","The southern region or area; the inhabitants thereof. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}"]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Toward the south; southward.","from the south."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/south"},{"term":"rim","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-3 language code for Nyaturu."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An edge around something, especially when circular.","A wheelrim."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rim"},{"term":"trail","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To follow behind (someone or something); to tail (someone or something).","To drag (something) behind on the ground."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The track or indication marking the route followed by something that has passed, such as the footprints of animal on land or the contrail of an airplane in the sky.","A route for travel over land, especially a narrow, unpaved pathway for use by hikers, horseback riders, etc."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/trail"}],"entries":[{"title":"Rim Trail","blocks":[{"text":"The Rim Trail is a hiking trail located on the South Rim of the Grand Canyon National Park, located in the U.S. state of Arizona. It is a 13 miles (21 km) trail between the South Kaibab Trailhead west to Hermit's Rest. It is also where former Major League Baseball player Charlie Haeger was found dead on October 3, 2020, which happened to be a day after his ex-girlfriend was found dead in Scottsdale, Arizona"}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rim_Trail"},{"title":"Grand Canyon National Park","blocks":[{"text":"Grand Canyon National Park is a national park of the United States located in northwestern Arizona, the 15th site to have been named as a national park. The park's central feature is the Grand Canyon, a gorge of the Colorado River, which is often considered one of the Wonders of the World. The park, which covers 1,217,262 acres of unincorporated area in Coconino and Mohave counties, received more than 4.9 million recreational visitors in 2024. The Grand Canyon was designated a World Heritage Site by UNESCO in 1979. The park celebrated its 100th anniversary on February 26, 2019."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/aa/Dawn_on_the_S_rim_of_the_Grand_Canyon_%288645178272%29.jpg/330px-Dawn_on_the_S_rim_of_the_Grand_Canyon_%288645178272%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Grand_Canyon_National_Park"},{"title":"South","blocks":[{"text":"South is one of the cardinal directions or compass points. The direction is the opposite of north and is perpendicular to both west and east."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9a/Compass_Rose_English_South.svg/330px-Compass_Rose_English_South.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/South"},{"title":"Trail","blocks":[{"text":"A trail, also known as a path or track, is a dirt road or a small paved road, usually through an undeveloped natural area, that is designed primarily for use by pedestrians, equestrians and non-motorized vehicles, although occasionally some off-roading motor vehicles may also use it. In the United Kingdom and Ireland, footpath or hiking trail is the preferred term. However, it is sometimes applied to highways in North America. In the United States, the term was historically used to describe the westward expansion trails, which are land routes into or through wildness regions of the American West used by explorers and migrants."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b0/Trail_between_two_fields_%28Slovenia%2C_Selo_pri_Mirni%29.jpg/330px-Trail_between_two_fields_%28Slovenia%2C_Selo_pri_Mirni%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Trail"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ef/USA_-_Arizona_-_Grand_Canyon_-_South_Rim_-_Hermits_Rest_Route_-_Panoramic_View.jpg/500px-USA_-_Arizona_-_Grand_Canyon_-_South_Rim_-_Hermits_Rest_Route_-_Panoramic_View.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ef/USA_-_Arizona_-_Grand_Canyon_-_South_Rim_-_Hermits_Rest_Route_-_Panoramic_View.jpg/1280px-USA_-_Arizona_-_Grand_Canyon_-_South_Rim_-_Hermits_Rest_Route_-_Panoramic_View.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ef/USA_-_Arizona_-_Grand_Canyon_-_South_Rim_-_Hermits_Rest_Route_-_Panoramic_View.jpg/500px-USA_-_Arizona_-_Grand_Canyon_-_South_Rim_-_Hermits_Rest_Route_-_Panoramic_View.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AUSA_-_Arizona_-_Grand_Canyon_-_South_Rim_-_Hermits_Rest_Route_-_Panoramic_View.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3e/Grand_Canyon_poster_1938.jpg/500px-Grand_Canyon_poster_1938.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3e/Grand_Canyon_poster_1938.jpg/500px-Grand_Canyon_poster_1938.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"1938 poster of the park","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AGrand_Canyon_poster_1938.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ad/ATBQ_2010_AZ_GrandCanyon.